      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Additional Experimental Details",
      "bbox": [
        128.58685302734375,
        73.71392822265625,
        293.97509765625,
        84.4616470336914
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "C.1",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        98.20179748535156,
        122.66494750976562,
        107.15817260742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Uncertainty Propagation using Lipschitz Continuity",
      "bbox": [
        132.62754821777344,
        98.20179748535156,
        353.85699462890625,
        107.15817260742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this section, we detail our implementation of the Lipschitz-based uncertainty propagation method",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        118.29632568359375,
        504.003173828125,
        127.20288848876953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which we compare with in Section 6. For these experiments, consider the dynamical system",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        129.205322265625,
        474.3746032714844,
        138.11187744140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xk+1 = f(xk) = h(xk) + g(xk),",
      "bbox": [
        210.71299743652344,
        146.9289093017578,
        350.6365966796875,
        157.26971435546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xk ∈Rn.",
      "bbox": [
        362.25799560546875,
        144.89016723632812,
        401.28961181640625,
        157.26971435546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(9)",
      "bbox": [
        492.384033203125,
        147.08831787109375,
        504.0003967285156,
        155.994873046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Note that we drop the dependence on the control input uk for conciseness, and since our comparisons",
      "bbox": [
        108.00003051757812,
        164.81190490722656,
        503.9996643066406,
        175.37188720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "concern a sequence of known open-loop controls. For simplicity, we assume h is an afﬁne map, and",
      "bbox": [
        108.00004577636719,
        175.7209014892578,
        503.9988708496094,
        184.786865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "g is Lipschitz continuous, such that for all x, µ ∈Rn,",
      "bbox": [
        108.00003051757812,
        185.08914184570312,
        323.77972412109375,
        195.69586181640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "|gi(x) −gi(µ)| ≤Lgi∥x −µ∥2,",
      "bbox": [
        208.77606201171875,
        203.95498657226562,
        342.3406066894531,
        214.88433837890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "i = 1, ..., n.",
      "bbox": [
        353.9669494628906,
        204.5128936767578,
        403.22955322265625,
        213.578857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(10)",
      "bbox": [
        487.40203857421875,
        204.67230224609375,
        503.99969482421875,
        213.578857421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The method presented in [13] consists of propagating ellipsoidal sets:",
      "bbox": [
        108.00003051757812,
        228.0343017578125,
        384.9403076171875,
        236.94085693359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deﬁnition 2 (Ellipsoidal Set). A set B(µ, Q), µ ∈Rn, Q ∈Rn×n, Q ≻0, is an ellipsoidal set if",
      "bbox": [
        108.00003051757812,
        240.83758544921875,
        494.3893737792969,
        251.83587646484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B(µ, Q) :=",
      "bbox": [
        209.6619873046875,
        261.5509948730469,
        257.68255615234375,
        270.9556884765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\b",
      "bbox": [
        260.4419860839844,
        260.554443359375,
        266.25018310546875,
        266.9305114746094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "x | (x −µ)T Q−1(x −µ) ≤1",
      "bbox": [
        266.2539978027344,
        257.9959411621094,
        392.0982666015625,
        270.9556884765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".",
      "bbox": [
        399.5699462890625,
        262.1089172363281,
        402.33953857421875,
        270.9556884765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(11)",
      "bbox": [
        487.4019470214844,
        262.268310546875,
        503.9996032714844,
        271.17486572265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Assume that xk ∈B(µk, Qk). The problem consists of computing µk+1, Qk+1 such that xk+1 ∈",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        285.9599914550781,
        504.00299072265625,
        297.0778503417969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B(µk+1, Qk+1). Generally, the reachable set of f(xk) given that xk lies in an ellipsoidal set will",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        296.8689880371094,
        503.9997253417969,
        307.9868469238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "not be an ellipsoidal set. However, an outer-approximation is sufﬁcient for control applications",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        308.49530029296875,
        504.0030822753906,
        317.40185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where constraints satisfaction needs to be guaranteed. First, we compute the center of the ellipsoid",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        319.404296875,
        504.0032653808594,
        328.31085205078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        330.31329345703125,
        116.29878234863281,
        339.2198486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "µk+1 = f(µk).",
      "bbox": [
        273.72296142578125,
        341.0628967285156,
        338.279541015625,
        351.4046630859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(12)",
      "bbox": [
        487.4019470214844,
        341.2222900390625,
        503.9996032714844,
        350.12884521484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Since h is afﬁne, its Jacobian does not depend on x. Thus, we decompose the error to the mean as",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        355.9569091796875,
        499.52593994140625,
        365.0228576660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xk+1 −µk+1 = h(xk) −h(µk) + g(xk) −g(µk)",
      "bbox": [
        200.4609375,
        373.281982421875,
        408.7824401855469,
        384.1816711425781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "= ∇h · (xk −µk) + g(xk) −g(µk).",
      "bbox": [
        259.0009765625,
        387.17999267578125,
        411.5416259765625,
        398.0796813964844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "First, given xk ∈B(µk, Qk), we have ∇h · (xk −µk) ∈B(0, Qnom,k), with Qnom,k = hQkhT .",
      "bbox": [
        108.00003051757812,
        409.38531494140625,
        495.7486572265625,
        423.18267822265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Second, we use the Lipschitz property of g to bound the approximation error component-wise as",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        429.22991943359375,
        493.1423034667969,
        438.2958679199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "|gi(xk) −gi(µk)| ≤Lgi∥xk −µk∥2 ≤Lgiλmax(Qk),",
      "bbox": [
        194.4550018310547,
        446.55499267578125,
        417.54656982421875,
        457.4833068847656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(13)",
      "bbox": [
        487.4019775390625,
        447.2723083496094,
        503.9996337890625,
        456.1788635253906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where λmax(Qk) denotes the largest eigenvalue of Qk, and since xk ∈B(µk, Qk). This deﬁnes a",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        464.43798828125,
        504.00274658203125,
        475.336669921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rectangular set in which g(xk) −g(µk) is guaranteed to lie, which can be outer-approximated by",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        475.34698486328125,
        503.9993591308594,
        485.66583251953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "an ellipsoid as",
      "bbox": [
        107.99995422363281,
        486.9732971191406,
        165.00595092773438,
        495.8798522949219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "g(xk) −g(µk) ∈B(0, Qgk),",
      "bbox": [
        119.32195281982422,
        504.13897705078125,
        239.53350830078125,
        515.1282958984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where Qgk = n · diag",
      "bbox": [
        251.1549072265625,
        504.13897705078125,
        341.9114990234375,
        516.0946655273438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0000",
      "bbox": [
        341.91192626953125,
        503.1424255371094,
        346.47479248046875,
        509.51849365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(Lgiλmax(Qk)2), i = 1, ..., n",
      "bbox": [
        346.4779357910156,
        502.6571044921875,
        468.7498779296875,
        515.0673217773438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0001",
      "bbox": [
        468.7459716796875,
        503.1424255371094,
        473.308837890625,
        509.51849365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ",",
      "bbox": [
        473.3129577636719,
        504.6968994140625,
        476.0825500488281,
        513.543701171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(14)",
      "bbox": [
        487.4019470214844,
        504.8562927246094,
        503.9996032714844,
        513.7628784179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where diag(...) denotes the diagonal matrix with diagonal components (...).",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        523.6258544921875,
        412.9295959472656,
        532.6918334960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Finally, the two terms can be combined as",
      "bbox": [
        107.99993896484375,
        540.1732788085938,
        275.4911804199219,
        549.079833984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xk+1 −µk+1 ∈B(0, Qnom,k) ⊕B(0, Qgk) ⊂B(0, Qk+1),",
      "bbox": [
        185.89093017578125,
        557.3389892578125,
        426.1104736328125,
        568.3292846679688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(15)",
      "bbox": [
        487.4018859863281,
        558.0562744140625,
        503.9995422363281,
        566.9628295898438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where Qk+1 = c+1",
      "bbox": [
        107.9998779296875,
        576.0040283203125,
        188.1929931640625,
        588.1936645507812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "c Qnom,k + (1 + c)Qgk, with c =",
      "bbox": [
        179.5850067138672,
        577.8529052734375,
        319.3268737792969,
        590.1357421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "p",
      "bbox": [
        322.71795654296875,
        576.030517578125,
        332.6805419921875,
        582.4065551757812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Tr(Qnom,k/Tr(Qgk), and Tr(·) denotes the",
      "bbox": [
        332.6809997558594,
        577.2950439453125,
        504.0003662109375,
        588.2853393554688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "trace operator. Finally, combining the terms above and by linearity,",
      "bbox": [
        107.99996948242188,
        588.92138671875,
        375.4060363769531,
        597.8279418945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xk+1 ∈B(µk+1, Qk+1).",
      "bbox": [
        255.39697265625,
        606.0870361328125,
        356.6045227050781,
        616.9866943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(16)",
      "bbox": [
        487.40191650390625,
        606.8043212890625,
        503.99957275390625,
        615.7108764648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Starting from x0 ∈B(µ0, Q0), and applying this recursion for all k = 0, ..., N−1, this method",
      "bbox": [
        107.99990844726562,
        629.4500732421875,
        503.9979553222656,
        640.3487548828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "enables the computation of sequence of sets which outer approximate the true reachable sets of the",
      "bbox": [
        107.9998779296875,
        641.0763549804688,
        504.00311279296875,
        649.98291015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "nonlinear system, given known upper-bounds for the Lipschitz constant of the dynamics.",
      "bbox": [
        107.9998779296875,
        651.9853515625,
        461.6122741699219,
        660.8919067382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "14",
      "bbox": [
        301.01885986328125,
        743.1333618164062,
        310.9814453125,
        752.0399169921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
  ],
